{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedTheta","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedTheta","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeSeminormalWeight"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_twist_eq_theta_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_twist_eq_theta_sq","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedTheta.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**The agreement, stated as one equation.**  The Jucys–Murphy product of the content eigenvalues\non `e₀` equals `θ_{(2,1)}²`, on a 2-dimensional module.\n\nLeft side computed from the JM spectrum; right side from the content sum of the partition. They are\nthe same, and `stdTwo_fullTwist_eq_one` reaches it a third way from the matrices alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_twist_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_twist_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedTheta.lean#L92-L97","doc":"**The two routes agree.**  The Jucys–Murphy product of the eigenvalues on `e₀` is\n`1 · q² · q⁻² = 1`, and the full twist really is the identity.  Both sides are `θ_{(2,1)}²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwo_fullTwist_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwo_fullTwist_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedTheta.lean#L76-L90","doc":"**The falsifiability check.**  `(σ₀σ₁)³ = 1` for the explicit `2×2` seminormal pair, by direct\nmatrix computation — no Jucys–Murphy input whatsoever.\n\nThis is the same number `θ_{(2,1)}² = 1` predicts, reached by a completely different route, so §1's\nconclusion is constrained by an independently-proved case rather than free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.theta_two_one_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.theta_two_one_sq","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedTheta.lean#L64-L68","doc":"Hence `θ_{(2,1)}² = 1`: the full twist of `B₃` is predicted to act **trivially** on the\nseminormal vector of the 2-dimensional block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.contentSum_two_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.contentSum_two_one","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedTheta.lean#L61-L62","doc":"`c((2,1)) = 0 + 1 + (−1) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.twistB_scalar_eq_theta_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.twistB_scalar_eq_theta_sq","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedTheta.lean#L46-L57","doc":"**The twist scalar is pinned, not merely permitted**, on a bounded presentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwistB_smul_eq_theta_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwistB_smul_eq_theta_sq","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedTheta.lean#L38-L44","doc":"**The full twist acts by `θ_λ²`** on a bounded presentation.  `prod_jmEigen` is reused verbatim\n— it never mentioned a presentation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}